\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: ETL/ELT process support\par
COMMENT:  Microsoft Fabric excels at moving and transforming data with multiple built-in tools that work for both simple and complex scenarios.  It offers visual pipelines and dataflows as well as advanced coding options for more control.  Lakehouse acts as the logical ingestion destination for ETL/ELT within the fabric stack\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/data-factory-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/data-factory-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/lakehouse-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/lakehouse-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA:  Standard Connectors & Adapters\par
COMMENT:  Fabric has over 150 pre-built connectors inherited from Azure Data Factory.  It connects to most major databases, cloud services, and business applications without custom coding. While Fabric offers broad connectivity, the quality and capabilities of these connectors aren't uniform.\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/data-source-management }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/data-source-management\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA:  API Support\par
COMMENT:  Fabric pipelines and dataflows can be created, triggered, and monitored through REST APIs, which supports automation and external integration. Some newer features and administrative functions still rely more on the user interface than APIs and lack full programmatic access.\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/fabric/articles/using-fabric-apis }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/fabric/articles/using-fabric-apis\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/pipeline-automation }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/pipeline-automation\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/lakehouse-api }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/lakehouse-api\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT: Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: Data Standard Support\par
COMMENT:  Fabric natively handles all modern data formats including JSON, XML, CSV, Parquet, and Delta Lake, ensuring compatibility across diverse systems. \par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/real-time-intelligence/event-house-connectors }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/real-time-intelligence/event-house-connectors\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: Metadata Management\par
COMMENT:  Fabric has robust built-in cataloging that automatically captures technical details about all data assets. Microsoft Purview, the governance part of the Fabric stack, enables lineage tracking and tracing information flows.  \par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/metadata-scanning-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/metadata-scanning-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/lineage }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/lineage\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/concept-data-lineage }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/concept-data-lineage\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT: Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: Data Exchange Protocols\par
COMMENT:  Fabric supports modern protocols like REST, HTTPS, and SFTP which work natively, along with real-time streaming through Event Hubs and Kafka-compatible interfaces. Support for older or niche transfer styles depends on the available connectors.\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/real-time-analytics/event-streams/overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/real-time-analytics/event-streams/overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-sftp-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/connector-sftp-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
