\par
DATA PRODUCT: Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: Data Profiling\par
COMMENT:  Fabric provides Dataflow Gen2, a visual tool that automatically generates statistics about data patterns and quality issues. Fabric relies on Microsoft Purview to profile data sources for governance.  Fabric's data profiling is useful for basic visibility, but is not a full data quality or monitoring solution.  \par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/unified-catalog-data-quality-profiling }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/unified-catalog-data-quality-profiling\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/dataflows-gen2-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-factory/dataflows-gen2-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT: Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA: Data Cleansing\par
COMMENT:  Fabric tools (such as Data Wrangler) and visual transformations with Fabric support common cleanup tasks like filtering and standardizing values. More advanced cleanup often needs code-based processing.\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-science/tutorial-data-cleaning-functional-dependencies }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-science/tutorial-data-cleaning-functional-dependencies\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
