{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-science/data-wrangler }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-science/data-wrangler\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA:  Data Validations\par
COMMENT:  Basic data checks can be added to pipelines to confirm whether data meets expected rules and to handle failures. But there is no centralized place to define and manage these rules.  So, teams must build and maintain validations across multiple tools.\par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/data-quality-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/data-quality-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/microsoft-purview-fabric }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/governance/microsoft-purview-fabric\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/unified-catalog-data-quality-rules }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/unified-catalog-data-quality-rules\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA:  Data Quality Metrics\par
COMMENT:  Fabric doesn't include automated quality scoring or metric tracking features out of the box. Metric tracking (with seperate dashboards for visualization) must be built from scratch using notebooks or SQL queries. \par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/notebook-visualization }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/notebook-visualization\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
