\par
DATA PRODUCT:  Microsoft Fabric\par
SUBCRITERIA:  Scalability\par
COMMENT:  The Fabric service is designed to handle growing data volumes by scaling capacity rather than individual machines. It uses a using a capacity-based model based on the purchase computing units.  Results still depend on how capacity and workloads are desgined and managed. \par
LINKS:\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/fundamentals/microsoft-fabric-overview }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/fundamentals/microsoft-fabric-overview\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/spark-compute }}{\fldrslt{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-engineering/spark-compute\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22\par
